From: Cubieboard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
Date: Fri, 7 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dts: sun9i-a80-cubieboard4: disable mmc1 (WiFi SDIO) in U-Boot

U-Boot does not use the BCM4330 WiFi chip, so there is no reason to
bind mmc1 (mmc@1c10000, the SDIO host for WiFi) during boot.

When mmc1 is enabled in the U-Boot DTS without explicit MMC aliases,
the DM block layer assigns devnums by scan order:

  mmc0 (SD,   mmc@1c0f000) -> devnum 0
  mmc1 (WiFi, mmc@1c10000) -> devnum 1   <-- steals the slot eMMC needs
  mmc2 (eMMC, mmc@1c11000) -> devnum 2

However, sunxi board.c maps BOOT_DEVICE_MMC2 (eMMC) to
mmc_get_env_dev()=1, so U-Boot looks for the boot partition on "mmc 1".
With WiFi bound as devnum 1, this fails:

  Loading Environment from FAT... ** Bad device specification mmc 1 **

and distro_bootcmd falls through to PXE without ever scanning the
eMMC, rendering eMMC installs unbootable.

Disabling mmc1 removes it from DM binding, yielding:

  mmc0 (SD,   mmc@1c0f000) -> devnum 0   (BOOT_DEVICE_MMC1 -> mmc 0)
  mmc2 (eMMC, mmc@1c11000) -> devnum 1   (BOOT_DEVICE_MMC2 -> mmc 1)

Both SD and eMMC boot paths now resolve to the correct block device.

Signed-off-by: Cubieboard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
---
 arch/arm/dts/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts b/arch/arm/dts/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	non-removable;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &mmc1_pins {
